  "body": {
    "id": "thm:single-hazard-alternative",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Suppose \\(S_t=\\varnothing\\) for \\(t\\ne k\\) and \\(S_k=\\{j\\}\\), where \\(j\\in\\{k,k+1\\}\\cap\\{1,\\ldots,T\\}\\). Then \\(J_+(S_k)=\\{j\\}\\), \\(j_\\star=j\\), and the two branches of \\(\\text{thm:local-single-hazard-alternative}\\) specialize to the former singleton-hazard alternative: if \\(\\mathcal H_\\star(B)\\ne\\varnothing\\), the local rational reconstruction equals \\(Q\\) for every compatible positive law; if \\(\\mathcal H_\\star(B)=\\varnothing\\), the local witness consists of two legal strictly positive laws with equal observed laws and different endpoint intervention vectors. The conclusions hold for all specified finite alphabets, null allowed effects, and arbitrary transition ranks.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "T",
      "t",
      "d",
      "k",
      "j",
      "ell",
      "S",
      "B",
      "Q",
      "Jplus",
      "jstar",
      "Hset"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:local-single-hazard-alternative"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Under \\(S_k=\\{j\\}\\) with \\(j\\in\\{k,k+1\\}\\), \\(J_+(S_k)=\\{j\\}\\); hence \\(j_\\star=j\\) and \\(\\mathcal H_\\star(B)=\\{(d,\\ell):0\\le d<k,\\ j\\le\\ell\\le T,\\ \\ell\\in B_d\\}\\). Apply respectively the affirmative and negative active branches of \\(\\text{thm:local-single-hazard-alternative}\\). Its uniformity clauses give the alphabet, positivity, null-effect, and rank assertions.",
    "justification": "Compatibility corollary preserving the sealed open-question answer identity while exposing the stronger local-parent theorem.",
    "gap": "The former singleton-parent theorem is now an immediate specialization of the broader at-most-one-informative-hazard local alternative.",
    "consumer": "The sealed answer remains stable for graph-history and downstream dependency compatibility.",
